Protect your data — hide it inside the class and control all access.

Step 1 — Declare all fields private. 
Step 2 — Write a public getter for each field you want to expose. 
Step 3 — Write a public setter with validation.

class Person{
private int age;
}

Now here age is private, so we can't access it like p.age. Because data is protected.

Then how do we access it?
Using getter and setter methods.

Getter = READ data
Setter = CHANGE data

